Rāma answers Jābāli with steady reason --- Rāma rejects wrong act seeming right --- Rāma says conduct marks pure and impure men --- Rāma declares people follow king conduct --- Rāma praises truth as dharma root and heaven path --- Rāma vows to keep father forest promise --- Rāma rejects Kṣatriya code mixing right and wrong --- Rāma scorns expedient counsel and affirms forest offerings --- Rāma cites Indra and seers winning heaven by truth and rites
